        <article class="lesson-article">
            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 2</span><h1>Monolith to Microservices</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>30 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>The Strangler Fig Pattern</h2>
                    <p>Gradually replace parts of the monolith with microservices, like a strangler fig tree.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">1. Identify module to extract
2. Create new microservice
3. Route traffic to new service (via API Gateway)
4. Delete old code from monolith
5. Repeat</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Identifying Service Boundaries</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">Look for:
- Business capabilities (Orders, Inventory, Shipping)
- Data ownership (who owns this data?)
- Team structure (Conway's Law)
- Change frequency (what changes together?)
- Scaling needs (what needs to scale independently?)</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Anti-Corruption Layer</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Protect new service from legacy data models
public class LegacyOrderAdapter
{
    private readonly ILegacyOrderClient _legacyClient;

    public async Task&lt;Order&gt; GetOrderAsync(int id)
    {
        var legacyOrder = await _legacyClient.GetOrderAsync(id);
        
        // Transform legacy model to new domain model
        return new Order
        {
            Id = Guid.Parse(legacyOrder.OrderNumber),
            CustomerId = legacyOrder.CustId,
            Total = Money.FromCents(legacyOrder.TotalCents),
            Status = MapStatus(legacyOrder.StatusCode)
        };
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Database Decomposition</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">Strategies:
1. Shared database (temporary) → start here
2. Database views → read from new, write to old
3. Change Data Capture → sync between databases
4. Full split → each service owns its data</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use Strangler Fig for incremental migration.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Identify boundaries by business capability.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use Anti-Corruption Layer for legacy integration.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
